WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
- Well, we have a house full
of single moms and dads,

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.410
and a few of them would love to share

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.280
what they're going through
so we can weigh in,

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.600
I don't know if you want me to weigh in.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.600
But let's get to it!

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:10.220
So where's Desiree?

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.053
- Right here.

00:00:11.053 --> 00:00:12.395
- [Kelly] Hi, Desiree.

00:00:12.395 --> 00:00:14.295
- Hi, hey Kelly, nice to meet you.

00:00:14.295 --> 00:00:15.418
- [Kelly] Hi.

00:00:15.418 --> 00:00:20.030
- I have two kids and I've been
a single mom since day one.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.830
They're amazing children.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.500
But my brother always tells
me that I reward bad behavior.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.280
For example, if we're at a store,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.510
and they're like fussing
around and they tell me

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.050
to buy them something,

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.340
and I just kind of give
in and buy it for them

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:35.940
'cause I just don't want
to deal with it anymore.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:38.040
And I feel like I'm too soft and I have

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.083
a hard time disciplining them
and I'd just love your advice.

00:00:42.083 --> 00:00:43.829
- [Kelly] We're so different Desiree.

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:45.323
(all laughing)

00:00:45.323 --> 00:00:46.240
- Oh my God.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.290
- Yeah, they're about to be
pre-teens, so I need help,

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:51.620
like breaking this cycle and
bringing some balance back

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.453
to my life.

00:00:52.453 --> 00:00:53.286
- Oh my God,

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.820
that cycle is going.
- It's gone!

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.834
- It's like they're
taking advantage of me.

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:58.740
- Here's the thing, I will relate to,

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.230
and I think everybody can.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:02.280
Sometimes they just wear you down.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.050
You're just like, "I'm
just tired of having

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.530
this conversation."

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.397
You're exhausted, you're like,

00:01:07.397 --> 00:01:08.930
"I cannot believe you're surprised

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.720
that bedtime happens every night!"

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.350
Like, "Why are we having this argument?"

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.460
Like, and it wears you down.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.900
So I get why you kind of give in,

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.430
but I will tell you what,
literally my kids the other day,

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:20.810
they were fighting over,

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.460
'cause they do that thing where,

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.293
there's is a little different.

00:01:23.293 --> 00:01:25.250
Like they know that if
we go to a store, I set,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.083
I prep them.

00:01:26.083 --> 00:01:27.580
I say, "We're going in this store

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:28.720
and you're not getting anything.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.810
We're doing something for
somebody else," or whatever.

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:31.804
Or I prep them and say,

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:34.190
"Hey, if y'all want to grab
something, like little,

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.580
you can get one little
thing or something."

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.840
But I am big on prepping
them, 'cause if you don't,

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.690
that's when the nightmare happens.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:43.860
And also they were fighting
the other day over something

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:45.910
and they were so entitled
and they've got so many toys.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.226
And so I took that toy
straight to the trash.

00:01:49.226 --> 00:01:51.170
- That's what I'm talking about!

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.420
- I was like, "I'm sorry,
since neither one of you

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.500
knows how to share it, we
will give it to the garbage.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.760
I was like, and it's gone.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.850
- Until they go in the
garbage and get it out.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:02.792
- Oh, they won't go in the garbage,

00:02:02.792 --> 00:02:03.800
they hate that I make
them take the trash out.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:04.952
(Kelly chuckling)

00:02:04.952 --> 00:02:07.010
- Oh no, Joshua has pulled out
many toys from the garbage.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:07.843
- [Kelly] Oh really?

00:02:07.843 --> 00:02:09.810
- I threw his iPad away one day.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.445
Oh, I went and got that out.

00:02:11.445 --> 00:02:14.530
(audience laughing)

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.510
But I had to teach him a lesson.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:18.230
He was crying, He's like, "Oh my God!"

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:19.697
Soon as he went to bed, I was like,

00:02:19.697 --> 00:02:21.379
"Don't let me forget that iPad."

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:22.212
(audience laughing)

